/// Bindgen Module
///
/// libclang-driven C header binding generation.  Replaces the hand-rolled
/// byte-scanning C-header parser (`passes/c_header_import.cryo`,
/// `parse_c_functions` / `try_parse_c_func` / `c_type_to_annotation`) with a
/// real clang AST walk via the stable libclang C API.
///
/// Drives the inline `extern module name := "C" { #include <h> }` path: build
/// a translation unit, walk its cursors, and emit real Cryo declarations
/// (functions today; structs / unions / enums / typedefs as the engine
/// matures) into the `ExternBlockNode`.  This is also `PLAN.md` Stage 1's
/// parsing engine, landed early.
///
/// ABI prerequisite (PROVEN, 2026-06-25 Phase-0 spike): libclang passes and
/// returns small structs (`CXString` 16B, `CXCursor` 32B, `CXType` 24B) BY
/// VALUE.  Cryo's SysV x86-64 codegen handles these (DirectPair / Indirect+
/// SRet / Indirect+ByVal) correctly, including the >16B callee-side ByVal
/// callback prologue that `clang_visitChildren` requires.
///
/// Planned decomposition (activated as each lands across the next phases):
///   • Clang     — libclang FFI surface: the CX* by-value structs + the
///                 `extern` function declarations (thin `clang_bindings.h`).
///   • TypeMap   — CXType -> Cryo annotation mapper (replaces the old
///                 string-matching `c_type_to_annotation`): pointers, const
///                 (-> §1 `const T*`), fn-pointers `(Args) -> Ret`, fixed
///                 arrays, record/enum/typedef references.
///   • Importer  — TU build + `clang_visitChildren` walk + emit FunctionNode
///                 / struct / enum / typedef into `ExternBlockNode`; the entry
///                 that supersedes `CHeaderImport::run`.

namespace Compiler::Bindgen;

public module Clang;
public module TypeMap;
public module Importer;
public module Generator;
